1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,048
Your perfume is lying to the state right now, and that mistake is going to cost you everything.

2
00:00:06,348 --> 00:00:15,852
Every citizen sprays mandatory obedience at dawn. It keeps the city peaceful, quiet, and entirely under total control.

3
00:00:16,152 --> 00:00:23,424
I missed a spot on my left wrist today. Just a tiny inch of bare skin that refused the chemical blanket.

4
00:00:23,724 --> 00:00:33,780
Suddenly, the sterile hallways of my apartment building don't smell like lavender and compliance. They smell like raw, unfiltered panic.

5
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:41,256
Neighbors walk past me with dead eyes, their scent trails locked in perfect sync with the ruling central algorithm.

6
00:00:41,556 --> 00:00:50,508
Then a public scanner blinks red. Not because I committed a crime, but because my natural sweat smells like defiance.

7
00:00:50,808 --> 00:00:57,720
The perfume was never meant to keep us calm. It was a camouflage hiding the fact that we were already caged.

8
00:00:58,020 --> 00:01:05,220
Enforcement drones are outside my window now, tracking the scent trail of a mind that suddenly refuses to obey.

9
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:13,344
I raise my bare wrist to my face and inhale deeply. For the first time in my life, I smell like myself.

10
00:01:13,644 --> 00:01:19,908
If the scent is a warning flare, what does it mean when your own skin stops smelling like obedience?
